\subsection{\href{https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/nf.nickname}{Number field nicknames}}
\begin{definition}\label{nf.nickname}
\uses{}
The LMFDB supports \textbf{nicknames}, short human-readable names for
various fields.  Examples include:

\begin{itemize}
\item  ``$\texttt{Q}$'', for the rationals $\mathbb{Q}$,
\item  ``$\texttt{Qi}$'', for $\mathbb{Q}(i)$,
\item  ``$\texttt{QsqrtN}$'', for $\mathbb{Q}(\sqrt{N})$, as in Qsqrt-5 for $\mathbb{Q}(\sqrt{-5})$,
\item  ``$\texttt{QzetaN}$'', for $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_N)$, where $\zeta_N$ is a primitive $N$th root of unity,
\item  ``$\texttt{QzetaN+}$'', for $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_N)^+$; i.e. the maximal real subfield of $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_N)$ (equivalently, the field $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_N + \zeta_N^{-1})$).
\item  more generally, ``$\texttt{Q(s1, s2, ... ,sk)}$'', for the field generated by algebraic numbers $s_1,s_2,\dots,s_k$.
\end{itemize}

In the general syntax, each $\texttt{si}$ may be built using the functions $\texttt{sqrt}$ (or $\texttt{root}$) and $\texttt{cbrt}$, together with the usual arithmetic operations $\texttt{+}$, $\texttt{-}$, $\texttt{*}$, $\texttt{/}$, ^, and parentheses.  The usual constants $\texttt{i}$, $\texttt{zetaN}$ and $\texttt{phi}$ (for $(1 + \sqrt{5})/2$) are also supported.  Some examples include:  ``$\texttt{Q(sqrt2,sqrt3)}$'', ``$\texttt{Q(sqrt(1+sqrt2))}$'',``$\texttt{Q(cbrt(1+zeta7))}$'', and ``$\texttt{Q(5}$^$\texttt{(1/12))}$''.
\end{definition}


